From: g2code33 <269358183+g2code33@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 16:40:58 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Fix PDF/PPTX slide reader hanging forever on 'Loading
 Material...'
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Root cause: WebKit (and therefore WebKitGTK, which Tauri uses on Linux)
cannot reliably round-trip a Blob/File through IndexedDB. Storing one can
fail silently, and reading a previously-stored Blob back out can leave
.arrayBuffer() pending with no success, no error, and nothing to catch.
SlideReader called exactly that (.arrayBuffer() on a Blob fresh out of
IndexedDB) to sniff a file's type before showing it, so a hang there
left 'Loading Material...' spinning forever with no way to fail.

Two-part fix:
 1. storage.ts: saveFile() now always converts a Blob/File to raw bytes
    BEFORE it ever reaches IndexedDB, so nothing saved from now on can
    hit this failure mode. Added loadFileBytes(), a safe replacement for
    the repeated 'instanceof Blob -> arrayBuffer()' pattern scattered
    across call sites: it still accepts a legacy stored Blob, but bounds
    the read with a timeout instead of waiting forever, and rejects with
    a clear, actionable error on timeout.
 2. idbStore.ts: layered in a second, independent self-heal — every
    get/set/del/keys/etc. now races against a timeout and, like the
    existing reject-based self-heal, discards the connection and retries
    once on a fresh one if the operation never settles at all. This
    covers the sibling case where it's the IndexedDB connection itself
    (not a specific Blob) that's wedged.

SlideReader.tsx and StudyMaterials.tsx's PDF-to-text conversion now use
loadFileBytes() and surface a distinct, retryable error state instead of
leaving an infinite spinner when a load fails or times out.

Regression tests: idbStore hang self-heal (fake timers), saveFile/
loadFileBytes Blob-safety and timeout behavior, and a SlideReader test
proving the reader shows a Retry button + clear message instead of an
eternal spinner on failure. Full suite: 79 files / 816 tests passing,
tsc clean, build clean.

Co-authored-by: arena-agent <297053741+arena-agent@users.noreply.github.com>
